    "note": "Mean degree is held at 40 in every row, so the mean number of contacts per person is constant. R_star is the expected number of outside infections produced by one introduction and all the cases it causes inside its own group. Two effects oppose each other: larger groups amplify locally (mu rises, superlinearly once (s-1)*tau approaches 1) but consume the contact budget that reaches other groups (outside falls linearly). R_star is therefore NON-MONOTONE in group size, with an interior maximum. Concentrating contact is not uniformly worse; it is worse over a range and then self-limiting, because a group that has absorbed a person's whole contact budget can infect no one else.",
